<compatibility>
<note version="8.2" severity="warning">
Since Version 8.2, EAGLE supports online libraries. The ids
of those online libraries will not be understood (or retained)
with this version.
</note>
<note version="9.7" severity="warning">
Since Fusion, design files support named views saved in design. 
Named views found in the design will not be understood with this version. 
</note>
<note version="9.7" minversion="9.7.0" severity="warning">
Since Version 9.7.0 new layer stackup definition has been added,
which will not be loaded with this version.
</note>
<note version="9.7" minversion="9.7.0" severity="warning">
Since Version 9.7.0 new active CAMJOB file name has been added,
which will not be loaded with this version.
</note>
<note version="9.7" minversion="9.7.0" severity="warning">
Since Version 9.7.0 board construction lines has been added,
which will not be loaded with this version.
</note>
<note version="9.7" minversion="9.7.0" severity="warning">
Since Version 9.7.0 new design rule definitions have been added,
which will not be loaded with this version.
</note>
<note version="9.7" minversion="9.7.0" severity="warning">
This design uses inner layer routing restrictions on restrict polygons.
The restrictlayers attribute will not be understood in older versions,
and the polygons will only restrict the top or bottom layer based on their layer assignment.
</note>
<note version="9.7" minversion="9.7.0" severity="warning">
This design uses the unified restrict layer format where all restrict objects
reside on layer 41 (Restrict) with a restrictlayers bitset. Older versions
expect separate tRestrict (41) and bRestrict (42) layers and may not display
bottom restrictions correctly.
</note>
</compatibility>
</eagle>
